1
00:00:00,373 --> 00:00:04,543
(Bernadette:)...I probably would have gone
into physics or ice dancing.

2
00:00:05,337 --> 00:00:08,217
(Leonard:)My tests of the Aharonov-Bohm
quantum interference effect...

3
00:00:08,381 --> 00:00:10,131
(Leonard:)...have reached an interesting point.

4
00:00:10,342 --> 00:00:12,722
We're testing phase shift
due to electric potential.

5
00:00:12,886 --> 00:00:15,096
(Bernadette:)-That's amazing.
SHELDON [CHUCKLES]: Yes.

6
00:00:15,263 --> 00:00:17,893
(Sheldon:)Leonard's work is nearly
as amazing as third graders...

7
00:00:18,058 --> 00:00:21,268
(Sheldon:)...growing lima beans
in wet paper towels.

8
00:00:22,270 --> 00:00:24,610
While I appreciate the "oh, snap"...

9
00:00:24,773 --> 00:00:28,063
(Sheldon:)...I'm uncomfortable having
your moist breath in my ear.

10
00:00:31,571 --> 00:00:34,781
(Bernadette:)Are you going to try to set up
the voltages using tunnel junctions?

11
00:00:35,867 --> 00:00:36,947
(Leonard:)Yes, I am.

12
00:00:37,118 --> 00:00:40,408
-Wanna see a simulation on my laptop?
-Oh, yeah. Show me.

13
00:00:40,747 --> 00:00:44,997
(Bernadette:)In microbiology, the most exciting thing
I get to work with is yeast.

14
00:00:46,253 --> 00:00:47,833
SHELDON: Howard?
-Yeah?

15
00:00:48,004 --> 00:00:50,594
(Sheldon:)Your shoes are delightful.

16
00:00:53,009 --> 00:00:55,299
(Sheldon:)Where did you get them?

17
00:00:55,762 --> 00:01:05,022
(Bernadette:)-What?
-Buzzinga. I don't care.

